 1      Introduction
 1.1     Background
     Music has had a profound effect on humans and societies throughout history. The evolution of
 music occurs constantly, influenced by advanced technology, personal experiences, social events,




                                                                                   型
 etc. The internal influence between artists also accounts for the music changes. Analysis of music
 is usually deemed relatively perceptual and subjective. However, music that is more abstract in
 itself can be quantified by various characteristics, which makes it possible for us to analyze the




                                                                 模
 music systematically and objectively.
     One of our goals in this paper is to develop appropriate measures to quantify the influence




                                                                学
 and similarity of music. Based on the quantification, more thorough analyses could be conducted,
 including identifying the significant artists and characteristics. We believe that a better understand-
 ing of the music evolved could be also be obtained with a series of carefully designed models and




                                                        数
 experiments.

 1.2     Restatement of the Problem
                                         ：

                                                                    els
     The analysis of music influence involves detail ranging from methods for quantification to
 identification of decisive factors. Thus, in order to analyze the influence of music in a clear and
                                        号
 systematic way, we restate the problem as follows.




                                                                  od
                                众

       • Develop a measurement of music influence between artists, and construct a directed influence
                                                                 m
         network that connects influencers and followers accordingly;
                        公


                                                    H
       • Quantify the music similarities and compare the music similarities between and within genres;

       • Testify whether there are significant differences between the distributions of within-genre
                                                 AT
        信




         and between-genre similarities;

       • Discover the decisive music characteristics that distinguish genres;
       微

                                          M



       • Determine the most contagious music characteristics among artists;
                                 ：




       • Identify the revolutionary artists, and analyze the evolution of music.
                         号




 1.3     An Overview of Our work
     To address the problem, this paper proposed five models to solve the respective sub-problems.
                 信




 The rest of the paper is structured as follows. Section 2 states a thorough problem analysis and our
 motivations. In Section 3, we give the assumptions and notations of the model. Section 4 provides
         微




 sufficient details of our model. In Section 5, we test the proposed model. Section 6 analyzed the
 strengths and weaknesses of our model. At lat, a conclusion is given in Section 7. A one-page
 document to the ICM Society is given in the appendices???.




